## Root Cause Analysis & Prescribed Fix (AUTHORITATIVE — start here, do not re-trace)
A code investigation already traced this bug to its cause and prescribed the minimal fix below. This is the plan of record. Apply it; do NOT re-read the whole codebase to re-derive it.

The Acceptance Criteria above describe the desired END BEHAVIOR to VERIFY — they are NOT an implementation blueprint. Do not re-architect, split values, or add new fields/abstractions to satisfy an AC literally when the prescribed minimal fix already makes that AC pass. Implement the fix below; the ACs are how you check you got it right.

HARD RULES:
- Make the SMALLEST change that fixes the root cause. Fewer lines of code is always better.
- REUSE existing functions. Before writing any new helper, search the repo for an existing util/parser/formatter that already does what you need (use the CodeGraph tool documented below) and call it. Writing novel code when a helper already exists is a defect to be rejected in review.
- **src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx** (`ContentstackProvider`): Carrier — the provider already declares an onEntryChange prop and a useEffect to register it, but the current signature onEntryChange?: (callback: (entry: IContentstackContent) => void) => void (line 38) does not match the SDK's ContentstackLivePreview.onEntryChange which takes a no-argument callback. The useEffect on lines 62-71 also assumes the callback receives updated entry data, which the SDK does not provide. This must be corrected so the provider accepts and wires the SDK's () => void callback pattern, triggering a re-render that relies on the SDK's internal state update rather than a callback parameter.
  - **Minimal fix:** Change IContentStackProviderProps.onEntryChange type from (callback: (entry: IContentstackContent) => void) => void to () => void to match the SDK's ContentstackLivePreview.onEntryChange signature. Update the useEffect on lines 62-71: instead of calling onEntryChange(cb) with a callback that receives updated data, call onEntryChange() directly (the SDK registers its own internal callback). Inside the useEffect, after onEntryChange() is called, use a state counter or toggle to force re-render so components re-reading from context get fresh data. Remove the content dependency from the useEffect deps array to avoid re-registration loops.
- **src/pages/_app.tsx** (`MyApp`): Wiring site — this is where ContentstackProvider is rendered (line 74) but onEntryChange is NOT passed as a prop. The SDK's ContentstackLivePreview.onEntryChange callback must be wired here and passed to ContentstackProvider so that entry changes in the CMS trigger a re-render through the context pipeline.
  - **Minimal fix:** Import ContentstackLivePreview from '@contentstack/live-preview-utils' at the top of _app.tsx. Pass onEntryChange={ContentstackLivePreview.onEntryChange} as a prop to ContentstackProvider on line 74, changing it to <ContentstackProvider defaultContent={content} onEntryChange={ContentstackLivePreview.onEntryChange}>. This wires the SDK's callback to the context's re-render mechanism. ⚠️ UNVERIFIED: the helper named here (`ContentstackLivePreview`) was NOT found in the repo — treat it as a HYPOTHESIS, not fact. Confirm it exists with the CodeGraph tool before importing it; if it does not exist, do not invent it — solve the fix another minimal way.
- **src/services/contentstack.ts** (`Stack`): Setup site — the Contentstack Stack is created here with live_preview config, and ContentstackLivePreview.init is already called. The SDK is initialized and the live_preview block is already conditionally added to options. This is the foundation the rest of the wiring depends on.
  - **Minimal fix:** No edit required. The file already: imports ContentstackLivePreview (line 3), reads CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW/CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW_TOKEN/CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST env vars (lines 24-26), conditionally adds options.live_preview (lines 54-60), calls ContentstackLivePreview.init({ stack: Stack, ssr: false }) on lines 68-72, and passes live_preview param through query functions. The implementer must REUSE the already-initialized Stack export and the already-imported ContentstackLivePreview.
- **.env.local.sample**: Documentation site — the live preview environment variables (CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW, CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW_TOKEN, CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST) are already read in src/services/contentstack.ts lines 24-26 but are NOT documented in .env.local.sample. Content authors and developers need these documented to enable and configure live preview.
  - **Minimal fix:** Add the following three entries under the existing Contentstack section in .env.local.sample (after the CONTENTSTACK_FETCH_TIMEOUT line): CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW="" (enable flag, set to "true" to activate), CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW_TOKEN="" (management/preview token from Contentstack stack settings), CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST="" (preview host, e.g. https://api.contentstack.io for NA or https://eu-api.contentstack.com for EU). Follow the existing CONTENTSTACK_ prefix naming convention.
- **src/hooks/useContent.ts** (`useContent`): Consumer — this hook purely reads content from ContentstackContext via useContentstackContext (line 6) and provides getContentByKey. It has no own data-fetching logic. Once ContentstackProvider correctly triggers re-renders on entry change, this hook and all 18+ callers of useContentstackContext will automatically receive updated content without any changes to this file.
  - **Minimal fix:** No edit required. The hook purely consumes context. It will automatically benefit from the ContentstackProvider re-render wiring once onEntryChange is correctly connected in _app.tsx and the context signature is fixed.
- **jest.config.js**: This story adds @contentstack/live-preview-utils. jest.config.js is declared as a file a new dependency can force a change to. Investigate whether this package requires a change here, and record changeRequired accordingly.

