Follow this plan step by step:
1. Create `src/context/contentstackContext.tsx` — define and export `ContentstackContextProvider` component and `useContentstackPreview()` hook; parse `live_preview`, `content_type_uid`, and `entry_uid` from `window.location.search` via `URLSearchParams`; store `{ previewToken: string | null, contentTypeUid: string | null, entryUid: string | null }` in React state; expose value through `createContext`.

2. Modify `src/services/contentstack.ts` — add `LIVE_PREVIEW_MANAGEMENT_TOKEN` and `LIVE_PREVIEW_HOST` env reads; extend the Stack initialization (or `live_preview` config object) with `{ management_token: ..., enable: true, host: ... }`; export a helper `getPreviewParams(previewToken?: string, entryUid?: string, contentTypeUid?: string)` returning `{ live_preview: string, entry_uid?: string, content_type_uid?: string }` or `{}` when no token is present.

3. Modify `src/interface/content/page.ts` — add `PreviewParams` interface `{ live_preview?: string; entry_uid?: string; content_type_uid?: string }`; extend the existing page-fetch input/options type to include an optional `preview?: PreviewParams` field.

4. Modify `src/services/pageService.ts` — import `getPreviewParams` from `contentstack.ts`; thread `preview` params through every SDK query call (e.g., `Stack.ContentType(uid).Entry(entryUid).fetch({ ...query, live_preview, entry_uid, content_type_uid })`); ensure the return shape still satisfies the existing `Page` interface.

